Optimize this native combinational circuit (256-input combinational priority encoder with valid, encoded and one-hot outputs) for shorter mapped-cell maximum data arrival while respecting the mapped-area cap. Preserve its exact module name, input/output ports, widths, and behavior for every input value. No clocks, state, input restrictions, assumptions, or don't-cares may be introduced.
Functional contract: Evaluate WIDTH=256 and LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY=0, retaining original parameter names and defaults. All 256 input bits are arbitrary binary values. For nonzero input select the highest set index. Preserve EVERY output bit even when output_valid=0: all-zero input must produce valid=0, encoded=0 and output_unencoded=1, exactly as the original. Invalid outputs are NOT don't-cares. No new assumptions, state or masked invalid outputs. Proof covers only this fixed parameter instance.
Fixed top parameter overrides applied identically to reference and candidate: {"LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY": 0, "WIDTH": 256}.

All conditions use Yosys plus OpenSTA, SKY130HD TT 25C 1.80V, no physical wire parasitics, input transition 0.10 ns, output load 0.010 pF, and zero external I/O delays. Fixed mapping policy: hierarchy; flatten; synth -noabc; ABC script: strash; dretime; map; cleanup -i -o; buffer; upsize; dnsize; stime -p with fixed driver/output load. Baseline area is 8056.4768 um^2; the area cap is 8862.124480 um^2. A 100 ns virtual clock is a reporting reference only; optimize maximum data arrival rather than the virtual-clock slack. Every candidate must pass full functional equivalence and max-slew/max-capacitance checks with zero violations under the fixed library and constraints. These area, eligibility and tool conditions are supplied identically in every arm.

Yosys can restructure arithmetic. Source-level adder counts do not establish serial adder counts in the final mapped netlist. Propose one candidate and state what available evidence supports the suspected bottleneck. Timing estimates are hypotheses to be checked by EDA, not measurements.

Return one JSON object with candidate_rtl, bottleneck, rewrite, expected_timing_gain, area_or_other_cost, and functional_boundaries. candidate_rtl must be synthesizable Verilog; helper modules are allowed.

